# Instrument tool calls

Tool spans explain what an agent attempted outside the model. Record the tool name, sanitized arguments, result metadata, latency, and error state as a child of the generation or reasoning span that initiated it.

Keep secrets and unnecessary personal data out of span payloads. When a tool fails, preserve the error category and retry outcome so the trace distinguishes a provider failure from a bad model decision.

The same trace can contain model generations, retrieval, and multiple tool calls; use parent spans to keep the execution tree readable.

## Record a tool call

Wrap a tool function with `observe`, and its arguments, result, latency and any error are recorded as a child of the step that called it:

```ts
import { observe } from "uncoil-sdk";

const lookupOrder = observe(
  async function lookupOrder(orderId: string) {
    return orders.find(orderId);
  },
  { type: "tool" },
);
```

```python
import uncoil

@uncoil.observe(type="tool")
def lookup_order(order_id):
    return orders.find(order_id)
```

If an argument is sensitive, pass `captureInput: false` (`capture_input=False` in Python) so the arguments stay out of the trace while timing and errors are still recorded. When you already have the result and timing, record it with `toolCall` instead. See the [TypeScript SDK](/docs/typescript) and [Python SDK](/docs/python) guides.
